# core/data/talk/grammar/en/ask_answer.tlk - T5b: more answers to ASK_FACT, ASK_WHO, ASK_ADVICE,
# ASK_FAVOR and ASK_REPEAT: honest, evasive and silly. Owner: TK. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py;
# register: SCRIPT_STYLE.md. Kid-safe throughout; nothing romantic or suggestive here.

# ---- ASK_FACT: "is it true?" ----------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_fact.yes2 act: yes
  "Yes. I saw it myself. From behind a bush, but I saw it."
  "True. Every word. Except the long ones."
  "Yes, and it's even weirder than you heard."
  "Yup. Triple-checked it. Twice, because I lost count."
  "Absolutely. Put it on a plaque."
  "It's true. I wish it weren't, but it is."
  "Yes! Finally, someone asks the right question."
  "Oh, it's true. The Mayor swore on a hat."
  "Yes. That's not gossip, that's journalism."
  "Correct. You've just earned a gold sticker. Imaginary."
  "Sure is. My nana said so, and she's never wrong. Loudly."
  "Yes. I have a witness. And a duck."
  "Mm-hm. Quite true. Don't make a face."
  "Yes, and the rest is worse."
@rule core.ask_fact.no2 act: no
  "No. That's a rumour, and a bad one."
  "Nope. Whoever said that has never been right. Not once."
  "Not at all. Somebody's been telling stories."
  "No, no, no. Three nos, that's how sure I am."
  "False. I'd bet a biscuit. A whole one."
  "Wrong, but I admire the confidence."
  "Nope. And I'd know. I'm in the know."
  "No. It's a myth, like the quiet Tuesday."
  "Absolutely not. Who has been talking? Was it the Mayor?"
  "No. Though I wish it were true. It'd be funnier."
  "Not that I've heard. And I hear everything."
  "No! Where did you get that? A cereal box?"
  "No. Next question, I'm not feeling this one."
  "Nope, and thanks for asking before you told everybody."
@rule core.ask_fact.unsure2 act: answer
  "I've heard both. I believe whichever one I heard last."
  "Maybe. I wasn't there, but I've got a feeling about it."
  "Honestly? I don't know, and I'm not paid to find out."
  "That's one of those things. You know the kind. Can't say."
  "Could be. Could be not. I'd flip a coin, but I'd lose it."
  "I'd need more facts. I'm out of facts. I've got a few feelings."
  "Hm. Let me think. {.}Nope, still don't know."
  "Ask somebody who reads the news. I read the weather."
  "Don't ask me. I only know about soup and shoes."
  "It's complicated. It has a lot of layers, and one of them is lunch."
  "Half true. Which half? That's the fun part."
  "It depends how you hold it. Hold it sideways. Now yes."
  "Rumour says yes. Rumour also says I can fly. I can't."
  "I'd tell you, but I'd have to guess. Want a guess?"
@rule core.ask_fact.joke act: joke
  "True? In this town? Ha, you sweet summer child."
  "Is it true? Does it matter? Anyway, yes."
  "True! As true as the fog. Which is wet."
  "I'd say yes, but my nose grows. Look, it's growing. {.}It isn't, I checked."
  "That's a question for a lawyer. Or a duck. I'd go duck."
  "If it's true, I'm a banana. {.}Peel me, I guess."
  "True or false? Neither, it's a sandwich. It's got layers."
  "I'll answer that after my snack. The snack may take years."
@rule core.ask_fact.dismiss act: dismiss
  "I don't do facts before noon. It's a policy."
  "Facts? I'd rather not. They only cause trouble."
  "Why do you want to know? What are you planning?"
  "Next question. That one's got a wrong smell."
@rule core.ask_fact.voice act: answer
  "I'm so sorry, I truly couldn't say. Would you like a biscuit instead?" guard: polite
  "Yes. Done. Why are you still here?" guard: blunt
  "Yes, no, whatever. Look it up." guard: blunt
  "Fact: I don't know. This is the fact." guard: flat
  "It is as it is. Facts are facts. I've said it." guard: flat
  "TRUE! TRUE AS A TRUMPET! I'M NOT YELLING!" guard: loud
  "FALSE! LOUDLY FALSE! WRITE IT DOWN!" guard: loud
  "That requires evidence. I shall need a table." guard: serious
  "I won't speculate. I will, however, sigh meaningfully." guard: serious
  "Eh, probably. Don't sweat it either way." guard: easygoing
  "Could be, could be. Mostly could be. Pass the cheese." guard: easygoing
  "True in a way that's mostly a sock." guard: quirky
  "Yes, if you're a pigeon. No if you're a lamp." guard: quirky
  "Yes yes yes, no, yes, next!" guard: quick
  "True, hm, wait. {.}Don't tell me. {.}Yes." guard: slow
  "True, and I've the bunions to prove it." guard: elder
  "Back in my day we didn't ask that. We just knew." guard: elder
  "Yeah, no, wait, yeah. Don't make it weird." guard: teen
  "I mean, literally yes? Obviously? Ugh." guard: teen
  "Down home we'd know. Up here, who can say?" guard: hellborn
  "Truth has changed since I died. Mostly it's gotten louder." guard: ghost
  "At this hour? The truth sleeps. I'll check in the morning." guard: night
  "Sorry, you're a stranger. I say yes to be polite." guard: rel=stranger
  "Between you and me? Yes, don't repeat it. I'll know." guard: rel=best
  "Why would I tell you? You'd use it. Yes, it's true, ha." guard: rel=rival
@rule core.ask_fact.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: yes
  "Yes! I saw it! It was under the stairs!"
  "Yes! My friend told me! Don't tell my friend I told you!"
  "Yep! Probably! My teacher said so, or the other teacher."
  "Yes, it's true! Pinky promise! Both pinkies!"
@rule core.ask_fact.kid2 guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: no
  "No, that's not true! Who said that? Was it a duck?"
  "Nuh-uh, I'd know. I know EVERYTHING. A lot."
  "No way, that's silly! I laughed. Ha, see?"
  "Nope! That's a made-up! You made that up!"
@rule core.ask_fact.type act: answer
  "According to chapter nine: probably. I'd check the index." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
  "I read about it. Briefly. {.}Mostly the pictures." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
  "If it's true, don't wake me. If it's false, wake me later." guard: type=cozy_napper
  "Yes? No? {.}I'll decide after my next nap." guard: type=cozy_napper
  "Of course it's true. Everything's true. That's what's wrong with everything." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
  "No. Because I say so. Because I say it." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
  "True, or maybe not. Who's to say. I'm not." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
  "It happened. Or it didn't. I went past it either way." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
  "I think so, yes. It felt true. Like a little bell." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
  "It's true in the dreaming. Out here, I'd have to ask." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
  "Yes, I believe it! I believe everything! It's lovely!" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
  "Oh, I hope so! I really do, {.}yes! Let's say yes!" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
  "Truth! A thing more fleeting than a sunset! {.}Yes." guard: type=dramatic_poet
  "True, my friend, and also tragic. Mostly tragic." guard: type=dramatic_poet
  "Would I lie to you? {.}Don't answer that. Yes." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
  "True. I wouldn't tell you a story. Not that kind, anyway." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
  "Verified. I've got it in the log. Page twelve." guard: type=diligent_helper
  "Let me check. {.}Checked, it's yes. Initialled." guard: type=diligent_helper
  "True! Heard it at a campfire. Everything at a campfire is true." guard: type=chill_adventurer
  "Yup. Or the other one. I'm pretty relaxed about which." guard: type=chill_adventurer
  "Affirmative, confirmed. Reported. Done." guard: type=stern_captain
  "Negative. I've checked the roster. It's wrong." guard: type=stern_captain
  "True, false! {.}Spin the wheel! {.}True!" guard: type=wild_card
  "I'd say yes, but then I'd have to prove it. So: sure!" guard: type=wild_card
  "Yes! And I've got a plan to make it truer!" guard: type=eager_go_getter
  "Yes, checking, {.}confirmed! Next question! Next!" guard: type=eager_go_getter
  "Yes, it's true! I just decided! Sparkly!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
  "Ooh, tell me it's true! {.}It's true!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
  "Yes. And anyone who says otherwise answers to me." guard: type=fiery_leader
  "It's true. Spread the word. Gently, then loudly." guard: type=fiery_leader
  "Yes! No! {.}I broke it, but yes!" guard: type=chaos_goblin
  "True, probably. I tested it with a hammer. A tiny one." guard: type=chaos_goblin

# ---- ASK_WHO ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_who.gossip2 act: gossip
  "Who? Somebody tall. Or somebody who stood on something."
  "I heard it was somebody with a hat. That narrows it to everyone."
  "Not telling. I'm a vault. A leaky vault."
  "Ooh, you want names? Come closer, {.}closer. {.}Too close."
  "The one with the thing. You know. The thing."
  "I can't say. But I can say 'hmm', in a way that says it."
  "Someone very close to the situation. And far from the exit."
  "Honestly? Half the town. The other half was napping."
  "A little bird told me. The bird was me. Don't tell the bird."
  "Everyone knows, and nobody will say. That's the system."
  "A person. A real, actual person. I've said too much."
  "It's a secret. I'd tell you, but I've forgotten it."
  "They have a funny walk and a nicer hat. {.}That's all you get."
  "I could point, but pointing's rude. {.}I'll point with my elbow."
@rule core.ask_who.other2 guard: other act: gossip
  "Try {other}. {other:cap} has opinions on this, and a notebook."
  "Don't tell {other} I told you. {other:cap} talks. Constantly."
  "If anyone knows, it's {other}. {other:cap} was there. Taking notes."
  "{other:cap}. Definitely {other}. {other:cap} gets everywhere."
  "I'd say {other}. Then I'd say it wasn't. Then I'd hide."
  "Ask {other}. {other:cap} owes me a favour. Make it a big one."
  "My bet's on {other}. Not my money, just my gut."
  "{other:cap} knows. {other:cap} always knows. It's slightly rude."
  "You'll want {other}. Go now. Take a snack."
  "Ooh, {other}'s the one. Ask nicely, {other} bites."
@rule core.ask_who.dismiss2 act: dismiss
  "That's not for me to say. Or for me to hear."
  "I don't know, and I'd rather not know. It's calmer."
  "Names are rude. I'm politely not doing them."
  "Who? Don't ask me who, ask me what. What I'll say is no."
@rule core.ask_who.joke act: joke
  "Who? Me, always me. I'm everywhere."
  "Who's who? Who knows? Who's on first?"
  "It was the Colonel, in the library, with the candlestick. {.}Wrong town."
  "It was the butler. We don't have a butler. {.}Yet."
  "Who? I'd say a name, but they're all taken."
@rule core.ask_who.voice act: gossip
  "Oh, I wouldn't dream of naming anyone. How terribly rude." guard: polite
  "Everybody and their dog. Pick one." guard: blunt
  "It's them, whoever. Doesn't matter. Done." guard: blunt
  "Someone did it. That's the end of what I know." guard: flat
  "I DON'T KNOW BUT I'M WILLING TO SHOUT ABOUT IT!" guard: loud
  "I'll tell you after I've verified it with three sources." guard: serious
  "Oh, somebody. Doesn't matter. It'll all come out in the wash." guard: easygoing
  "The one who sneezes in colour." guard: quirky
  "Them, her! Him, whatever! Gotta go!" guard: quick
  "Well.., {.}it was... {.}I've forgotten. {.}Come back later." guard: slow
  "In my day, we knew who. And we said nothing. For decades." guard: elder
  "Ugh, like, everyone? Obviously? I can't." guard: teen
  "Probably the one with the horns. It's usually the one with the horns." guard: hellborn
  "I saw it all. Nobody looked at me. That's the best part of being dead." guard: ghost
  "In the dark? I couldn't see their face. It had a hat." guard: night
  "I don't know you. I won't tell you. No offence." guard: rel=stranger
  "You and me, best friends: it was {other}, but never tell." guard: rel=best&other
  "You'd love that, wouldn't you? Well, no. Ha." guard: rel=rival
@rule core.ask_who.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: gossip
  "I know, I'm not telling! It's a secret, {.}it was a girl. Or a boy."
  "Somebody big! With big shoes! That's all I'll say!"
  "I saw them! They were really, really quiet!"
  "Not me! I wasn't even there! Don't look at me!"

# ---- ASK_ADVICE -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_advice.plain2 act: answer
  "Take a walk. If it doesn't help, take a longer walk."
  "Eat something warm. Most problems are cold ones."
  "Make a list. Cross off the easy bit. Feel great."
  "Ask somebody you trust. Then ignore them. Then ask again."
  "Whatever you pick, pick it loudly. It helps."
  "Sleep on it, and also on the couch. Different thinking happens on the couch."
  "Do the thing you'd do if nobody was watching. Then close the curtains."
  "Start small, wiggle a toe. Then another toe. That's a plan."
  "Take it one step at a time. And one biscuit at a time."
  "When in doubt, tidy something. It's not an answer, but it's something."
  "Go and ask the fog. It always has a view."
  "Don't decide on an empty stomach. Don't decide on a full one either."
  "Be kind. Then be kind again. Then see what happens."
  "If it's scary and you're curious, go. If it's scary and you're not, don't."
@rule core.ask_advice.encourage2 act: encourage
  "Do it. If you fall, I'll put a cushion down. After."
  "You're braver than you think. I'm braver than I think, too. Don't test me."
  "I believe in you. I've got a banner. It says 'you'."
  "Go, shine! Trip a little! It's part of it!"
  "You've survived every bad day so far. That's a hundred percent record."
  "Try, mess up. Try again, messier. It's the method."
  "I'd back you in any contest. Even sitting."
  "Just do the next small thing. I'll cheer."
@rule core.ask_advice.joke act: joke
  "My advice? Don't take advice from somebody who ate a candle."
  "Sell everything, buy a goat. {.}I'm not a lawyer. Or a goat."
  "Flip a coin. If it's heads, do it. If tails, flip again."
  "Don't, {.}well, do. {.}Hm. {.}Do the other one."
  "Advice costs a biscuit. Good advice costs two. This is a three."
@rule core.ask_advice.dismiss act: dismiss
  "Don't ask me. I put my socks on the wrong feet."
  "I'm the wrong person. Try someone with a plan. Or a hat."
  "If I had advice I'd keep it. It's lonely out there."
@rule core.ask_advice.voice act: answer
  "If I may: be gentle with yourself. And with the soup." guard: polite
  "Stop whining. Do something." guard: blunt
  "Just do it. Or don't. But stop asking." guard: blunt
  "Advice: do the thing. Or not the thing." guard: flat
  "DO IT, GO, RIGHT NOW! IN A MINUTE! SIT DOWN FIRST!" guard: loud
  "Consider every consequence. Then consider the biscuit." guard: serious
  "Don't stress. It'll sort itself out. It always does, eventually." guard: easygoing
  "Ask the nearest pigeon. If it nods, go." guard: quirky
  "Go, do, fix, done. Next." guard: quick
  "Well.., {.}mm. {.}Sleep on it. {.}Then sleep on it again." guard: slow
  "At my age I've learned one thing: wear the warm socks." guard: elder
  "Ugh, I don't know. Just don't be weird about it." guard: teen
  "Burn the bridge. {.}No, wait, that's a down-home answer. {.}Build a bridge." guard: hellborn
  "Be bolder than I was. I regret nothing. {.}Fine, one thing." guard: ghost
  "Ask me in the morning. Night advice is mostly nonsense." guard: night
  "We've only just met. My advice: don't ask strangers." guard: rel=stranger
  "For you? Honest answer, take the thing you want. Be nice, bring snacks." guard: rel=best
  "Take my advice? You? Ha, {.}fine, here, it's free." guard: rel=rival
@rule core.ask_advice.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: answer
  "Share your snack. Say sorry. Wear a coat."
  "Ask a grown-up! A good one! With cookies!"
  "Be brave! And if you can't, be brave next time!"
  "Hug a pillow. Count to ten. Count to ten again."
  "Tell the truth. Then run, if it's the scary kind."
@rule core.ask_advice.type act: answer
  "Read up on it. If it's not in a book, make a book." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
  "Hold on. Let me find the right page. {.}It's all of them." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
  "Lie down first, then decide. It works wonders." guard: type=cozy_napper
  "Best advice is a blanket and a cup of something. Then ask again." guard: type=cozy_napper
  "Complain a bit. Then do it anyway. That's how I get by." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
  "Advice? You wouldn't listen, nobody listens. {.}Fine: stop thinking so loud." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
  "Eh. Drift a bit. The answer finds you." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
  "Do what you were going to do. Pretend it was your idea." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
  "Follow the nicest feeling. It knows the way." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
  "Listen to the quiet bit inside you. It's been waiting." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
  "Be yourself! And if that fails, be a nicer self! Hee!" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
  "Smile at someone! Anyone! It fixes SO much!" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
  "Follow your heart, dear friend, though it lead you over a cliff!" guard: type=dramatic_poet
  "Write it down as a poem. It'll make no sense, and you'll feel better." guard: type=dramatic_poet
  "Be confident. If that fails, be charming. If that fails, be confident again." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
  "Smile like you know something. It's most of the job." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
  "Make a schedule. Start with 'breathe'. Tick it off." guard: type=diligent_helper
  "Break it into steps. Then break the steps into smaller steps." guard: type=diligent_helper
  "Take a hike. Literally. It all looks smaller from a hill." guard: type=chill_adventurer
  "Pack light, go far, take a snack. That's most of life." guard: type=chill_adventurer
  "Stand straight, face it. Then do it. In that order." guard: type=stern_captain
  "Discipline. A little every day. And a sandwich." guard: type=stern_captain
  "Pick one at random! Don't second-guess! Spin!" guard: type=wild_card
  "Do the opposite of what you planned. It's a good surprise." guard: type=wild_card
  "Go big, faster! Then go bigger! I'll hold your coat!" guard: type=eager_go_getter
  "Make a goal, then a bigger goal, then a snack goal." guard: type=eager_go_getter
  "Do something sparkly! Sparkle fixes all!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
  "Dance about it! Seriously! Dance!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
  "Decide, then lead. Others will follow. Or I'll ask them." guard: type=fiery_leader
  "Own it. Whatever it is. Own it and move forward." guard: type=fiery_leader
  "Try the silliest solution first. It's often the right one." guard: type=chaos_goblin
  "Take it apart and put it back wrong. You'll see." guard: type=chaos_goblin

# ---- ASK_FAVOR ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_favor.yes2 act: yes
  "Happy to. I've nothing better to do. {.}That came out wrong, I'm happy."
  "Sure thing. I'll even do it with a smile. A small one."
  "Yes. It'll cost you one biscuit. {.}Kidding, half a biscuit."
  "Of course! I live for this. And for snacks, mostly snacks."
  "Yeah, I'll do it. Don't make it a thing. {.}Make it a small thing."
  "Okay! One favour, coming up. Ask me again later for a bonus."
  "Absolutely. I'll even wear my helpful hat."
  "Done. Consider it done. I'll consider it harder tomorrow."
  "Yes! Favours are my love language. {.}Or biscuits, either."
  "Okay, you owe me. I keep a tab. It's written in crayon."
@rule core.ask_favor.no2 act: no
  "I'd love to, but my calendar says no. In crayon."
  "No, sorry. It's not you. It's the thing you asked."
  "Can't. I'm in the middle of a nap. It's a deep one."
  "No. And before you ask, no to the other one too."
  "Mmm, no. I'd do it badly. You'd be sad."
  "No. But I'll feel awful about it. That's something."
  "Not today. Ask me when the moon's out. And I'm in the mood."
  "No, thank you. It's a polite no, with a bow on."
  "No. I'd do it, but my knees have a veto."
  "No can do. I've a standing appointment with a chair."
@rule core.ask_favor.offer2 act: offer
  "I can't do that one. But I could hold your coat while you do."
  "Not that, but how about a snack? Snacks fix most favours."
  "That's beyond me. I'll cheer from the side."
  "I'll do half. You do the half I'm bad at."
  "I know someone who can. I'll go and look at them meaningfully."
  "Not me, but my hat could. It has connections."
@rule core.ask_favor.complain act: complain
  "Another favour? I haven't even finished the last one."
  "You ask a lot for somebody who gives so little. Biscuits. I mean biscuits."
  "Favours, favours. Nobody ever asks me how I am. {.}Fine, what is it?"
  "Fine, fine, but I'm going to sigh the whole way."
@rule core.ask_favor.voice act: yes
  "Certainly! It'd be my pleasure! Do let me know the details." guard: polite
  "Yes. Fine. Don't make a speech." guard: blunt
  "Okay. Done. Next." guard: blunt
  "Okay. I'll do it. This is me agreeing." guard: flat
  "YES, ABSOLUTELY! COUNT ON ME! CAN I SIT FIRST?!" guard: loud
  "Very well. I shall take it seriously. Please do the same." guard: serious
  "Sure, whatever you need. No pressure, no rush." guard: easygoing
  "Yes. I'll do it with a hop. Maybe two." guard: quirky
  "Yes yes yes, on it, go go go!" guard: quick
  "Yes.., {.}all right. {.}I'll get to it. {.}Soon, {.}ish." guard: slow
  "Of course, dear. Just hold my cane." guard: elder
  "Ugh, fine. But don't, like, make it weird." guard: teen
  "Yes. A favour for a favour. Down home that's law." guard: hellborn
  "Sure! I've got all the time in the world. And the next one." guard: ghost
  "At this hour? Fine. But I'll be a bit spooky about it." guard: night
  "I don't know you. But all right, just this once." guard: rel=stranger
  "For you? Anything, within reason. Within a biscuit's reach." guard: rel=best
  "You? Asking me? {.}Fine, but you owe me, big." guard: rel=rival
@rule core.ask_favor.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: yes
  "Okay, I'll help! I'm really strong! Look!"
  "Yes, can I use a big voice? Yes? Okay!"
  "Sure! Then can we play after? Pinky swear?"
  "Yes! I love helping! It's my best thing!"
@rule core.ask_favor.kid2 guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: no
  "No, I'm busy! Look, busy! I'm doing busy!"
  "Ask a grown-up! They're bigger!"
  "Nope! My mum says no strangers. {.}Or favours, or soup."
  "No, sorry. I have to be somewhere. Over there."
@rule core.ask_favor.type act: yes
  "I'd be glad to. But only if I can be quiet about it." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
  "Sure. Let me put a bookmark here first." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
  "Yes. After this nap. Or the one after." guard: type=cozy_napper
  "Okay, if I can do it from the couch." guard: type=cozy_napper
  "Fine. But I won't enjoy it. And I'll tell you." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
  "Ugh, fine. You owe me a grumble." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
  "Sure, whatever. I wasn't doing anything. I'm never doing anything." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
  "Yes, it's on my way. I don't have a way. But yes." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
  "Oh, of course. It sounds lovely. Everything does." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
  "Yes, if the clouds stay in a good mood." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
  "Of course, I'd love to! I love favours! And you!" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
  "Yay, a job! I'll do it so well! With sparkles!" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
  "Your wish is my command! And my sonnet! And my encore!" guard: type=dramatic_poet
  "A favour! At last, a purpose! Hold my cape." guard: type=dramatic_poet
  "For you? Sure. But I'm adding it to your account." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
  "Sure. I'll add it to the list of things I'm brilliant at." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
  "Of course! Noted, filed, and scheduled for Thursday." guard: type=diligent_helper
  "Absolutely. I've set an alarm. And a backup alarm." guard: type=diligent_helper
  "Sure, I'll bring a rope. And a snack. And a rope for the snack." guard: type=chill_adventurer
  "No worries. I'll get it done on the way up the hill." guard: type=chill_adventurer
  "Granted. Briefly. Report back when done." guard: type=stern_captain
  "Understood. I'll see to it. Stand by." guard: type=stern_captain
  "Hmm, sure! Spin a favour! What's the worst that can happen?" guard: type=wild_card
  "Yes, no! {.}Yes! The coin says yes!" guard: type=wild_card
  "Yes! I'll do it twice! For extra credit!" guard: type=eager_go_getter
  "On it! I'm already on it! I was on it before you asked!" guard: type=eager_go_getter
  "Yes yes yes! I'll make it sparkly!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
  "Ooh, a favour! Is there a ribbon? There should be a ribbon!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
  "Yes. Count on me. The rest of you: fall in." guard: type=fiery_leader
  "Done. Consider it handled. Who's next?" guard: type=fiery_leader
  "Yes! And I'll probably add a flourish. Or break it, hee!" guard: type=chaos_goblin
  "Sure, I'll do it my way. You won't like it. You'll love it." guard: type=chaos_goblin

# ---- ASK_REPEAT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_repeat.plain2 act: answer
  "I said: it's time for a snack. And it is. Always."
  "Wasn't important. You'd have hated it. Moving on."
  "Fine, again: I said it very, very well. Twice."
  "What did I say? Something wise. I've already forgotten it."
  "Sure. Let me gather my thoughts. {.}They've scattered, try tomorrow."
  "It was a joke. A good one. You missed the good part."
  "I said hello. In a way you didn't hear."
  "Nothing you need to know. Everything you want to know. Mostly nothing."
  "I'll say it louder. {.}I'll say it LOUDER. {.}Better?"
  "I said, 'what a nice day.' It isn't. I was being polite."
  "I mumbled. It's part of my charm. Here's a clearer one."
  "Oh, you want the whole thing again? Fine. Sit."
@rule core.ask_repeat.complain2 act: complain
  "I'm not repeating it. It wasn't any better the first time."
  "Do you know how hard it is to be this brilliant once? Don't ask for twice."
  "I said it once. It's still true. I'm not doing an encore."
  "You're making me say it again. Rude. Now I've lost my place."
  "Honestly. I speak, you wander off. This is how wars start."
  "I'll say it again, but I'm sighing the whole time."
@rule core.ask_repeat.joke act: joke
  "What? What did I say? {.}No, really, what did I say?"
  "I said 'repeat after me'. You didn't. That's the bit I'm cross about."
  "I said what I said, and I regret what I'm about to say."
  "Say what again? Hmm? {.}Now I've lost my own lines."
  "I'd repeat it, but I'm saving it for a rainy day. Look, it's drizzling."
@rule core.ask_repeat.voice act: answer
  "Of course! My pleasure! Let me say it more clearly." guard: polite
  "No, read my lips. Oh, you can't. I'm wearing a scarf." guard: blunt
  "I said it. You didn't hear it. Not my problem." guard: blunt
  "I said what I said. I will say it again. It is the same." guard: flat
  "I SAID IT ALREADY! BUT HERE IT IS AGAIN! LOUDER!" guard: loud
  "I'll repeat it once. Listen carefully. It's important." guard: serious
  "Sure, sure, no problem. Happy to go again." guard: easygoing
  "The same, but with a little hat on." guard: quirky
  "Said it. Saying it again. Fast, ready?" guard: quick
  "I said... {.}...hm, {.}give me a moment. {.}A longer one." guard: slow
  "Speak up, dear! {.}Oh, that was me. {.}What was I saying?" guard: elder
  "Ugh, do I have to? It was fine the first time." guard: teen
  "Again? It's no better the second time. Same fire, same smoke." guard: hellborn
  "I said it ghostly the first time. It's a gift. Again?" guard: ghost
  "Shh. At this hour I whisper. Come closer." guard: night
@rule core.ask_repeat.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: answer
  "I said: HI! And also: look at this stick!"
  "I forgot! It was about a bug! Or a bun!"
  "I said it! With my mouth! Out loud!"
  "Again? Okay, louder this time! HELLO!"
@rule core.ask_repeat.type act: answer
  "I said it softly, on purpose. Come closer. Not too close." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
  "It's in a footnote. I'll read it to you. Slowly." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
  "Zzz.., what? Oh. I said nothing, and it was cozy." guard: type=cozy_napper
  "I said 'five more minutes'. I'll say it again, in five." guard: type=cozy_napper
  "Nobody listens, then they ask again. Typical." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
  "I said what I said, and you heard it, you just didn't like it." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
  "Said something. Probably. It was a while ago." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
  "It's in the air somewhere. Catch it if you like." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
  "I said something soft. It floated off. I'll fetch another." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
  "It's just a feeling, really. I'll say it again slower." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
  "Of course! I'd say it a hundred times! It's lovely!" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
  "Yes, again! With a smile, ready? {.}Hello!" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
  "Oh, gladly! It deserves a second performance! Curtain!" guard: type=dramatic_poet
  "A fine line, worth a second reading. Brace yourself." guard: type=dramatic_poet
  "Missed it? Pity. I'll do it again, but it won't be as good." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
  "Again? Because you liked it. I knew you would." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
  "Certainly. I've got it in my notes. Page three." guard: type=diligent_helper
  "Of course. Let me find it. {.}Found, reading." guard: type=diligent_helper
  "Say again? Sure, I'll say it on the hike. Keep up." guard: type=chill_adventurer
  "No worries. I'll say it again. The echo's good here." guard: type=chill_adventurer
  "Pay attention. I'll repeat this once." guard: type=stern_captain
  "Listen up, again. The same. Don't make me do it twice." guard: type=stern_captain
  "I said something, or did I? Spin the wheel! {.}Let's find out!" guard: type=wild_card
  "I said it. Now I'll say it backwards, ready? {.}Gnihtyreve." guard: type=wild_card
  "Right, again! With more energy! One, two, three!" guard: type=eager_go_getter
  "Yes, repeat! Rehearse, improve! Repeat!" guard: type=eager_go_getter
  "Again, yay! I love it when it's twice! Twice!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
  "Okay! Sparkly version! Here we go!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
  "Listen, again, everyone. This is important. Ready?" guard: type=fiery_leader
  "Fine. Louder, so the back row hears it." guard: type=fiery_leader
  "I said something about a spoon. I'll say it again. With the spoon." guard: type=chaos_goblin
  "I said it, then I threw it. You missed it. I'll do it again." guard: type=chaos_goblin
